-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107: a WITHIN that reads a ledger, through a rule (or a
-- rule that names one), or with a RECALL of its own, and an OF anchor that
-- does, are not worked out: outside a run the ledger is empty, so the answer
-- would be the fallback whatever the run had recorded.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF pay

`recorded period` MEANS fromMaybe 10 (RECALL `period`)

`via another` MEANS `recorded period` PLUS 1

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`ledger read` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `recorded period` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`through another` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `via another` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`direct read` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN fromMaybe 10 (RECALL `period`) LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`direct anchor` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN 2 OF fromMaybe 3 (RECALL `start`) LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
